  "id": "thewash",
  "neon": "#7fe3ff",
  "note": "THE WASH — the launderette on the west side of Ironside Street, and the lowest thing on it.\n\nIt was the plainest building on the street by measurement rather than by opinion: four mass\nsegments, two wall palettes and a roof at 0.61, against a street whose next-plainest was 0.70.\n\n⚠ THE HEIGHT IS THE EXTRACT, NOT THE BUILDING. A launderette is one room and has no business being\ntall, so the shed stays low and what puts it on the skyline is the flue — which is also the only\nhonest answer to where the steam goes. The lantern over the machines is the same argument one\nstorey down: it is how a single-storey room with thirty tumble dryers in it gets any light at all.\n\n⚠ AND THE GLAZING IS ONE BAND WITH THE DOOR BESIDE IT, not a pair of punched windows. Everybody\ninside is waiting, so the whole frontage is a window with people sitting behind it, which is what a\nlaunderette looks like from the far pavement at ten at night.",
